<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue id="a5c3-8d4c-b6a2-f05f" name="Early Samurai" revision="5" battleScribeVersion="2.03" authorName="Jono Firth" library="false" gameSystemId="c749-87c2-0d4a-5e29" gameSystemRevision="12" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>This army list covers the later Heian period, through the Genpei War of the late 12th century, and up until and after the attempted Mongol invasions.

The list uses the japanese terms for weaponry; a katana is a sword; naginata is a pole arm treated as a bill; a daikyu is the samurai bow, treated as a long bow on foot and composite bow on horseback; the kyu is a composite bow. Armour uses the more familiar terms. The katana is treated as a hand weapon even though it was often used two handed. It is notable that katana-wielding Samurai are treated as expert swordsmen.

An Early Samurai must include a general and at least one unit of Samurai Infantry and one of Followers.</readme>
